**Raine.** A wandering swordsman seeking atonement for his years as an
assassin. Once a skilled assassin for the Clan Cave Fox, Raine broke
from the clan after discovering that a contract kill was, in fact, his
own estranged father. Disgusted with himself, he abandoned that
life -- but the clan doesn't let members leave, and dispatched his old
comrade Shou to hunt him down. Raine now wanders, trying to atone by
helping those he can. Reserved and thoughtful, Raine speaks only when
he has something worth saying, and his mind often wanders even when
he's paying close attention -- a habit that leads people to
underestimate him. He practices swordsmanship and origami in his spare
time, often folding paper to help himself think. *Agile +1, Art of
Invisibility +2, Attack +3 (Kaze Satsujinsha), Beautiful +4, Combat
Expert +4, Evasive +2, Intuitive +1, Iron-Willed +1, Knowledge +2
(Origami), Knowledge +2 (Wilderness), Quick +1, Sixth Sense +2,
Vigorous +2; Airhead −1, Code of Conduct −2 (Will Not Fight Surprised
or Defenseless Opponents), Guardian −2 (Those in Need), Ineptitude −3
(Home Economics), Pacifist −1, Poor −3, Rival −2 (Shou), Secret −2
(Past as an Assassin), Sensitivity −1 (Sexual Misidentification),
Unique Weakness −1 (Nightmares), Wanted −3 (Clan Cave Fox).* Kaze
Satsujinsha (Armor Piercing; Weapon): Roll 7, DX 4, End 0. Raine's
skill with a sword is extraordinary. His legendary katana is a
suitable companion. Raging Thunder Slash (Affinity: Electricity;
Effective x3; Weapon): Roll 7, DX 7, End 10. Raine whispers across his
blade before striking with crackling electrical energy. Electrical
Storm (Affinity: Electricity; Area Effect x2, Effective; Requirement:
Must Be Outside (−10), Weapon): Roll 7, DX 5, End 10. Raine summons
the power of nature to cut swaths through legions of enemies. Mist
Touch (Affinity: Spirit; Continued Effect, Fatiguing, Will Attack):
Roll 7, DX 4, End 10. Raine concentrates his energies to project his
very spirit into the opponent's mind. Defense 5. Health 40,
Endurance 60. TV 18.

